        "title": "refactor(agents): split embedded attempt orchestration",
        "body": "Closes #106302\n\nAI-assisted: implemented and reviewed with Codex.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe embedded agent attempt runner had grown to 5,868 lines and mixed bootstrap preparation, tool setup, system-prompt assembly, transcript repair, context summaries, and orphan-turn recovery in one module. That made focused runtime changes harder to review and increased conflict risk.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nExtract cohesive preparation and transcript responsibilities into seven focused helper modules while keeping attempt.ts as the orchestration owner. Call ordering, state flow, cleanup ownership, and runtime contracts remain unchanged; no compatibility layer or behavioral redesign is introduced.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Agent-runtime maintainers get smaller review surfaces: each new helper is 39–335 lines, and attempt.ts is reduced by 1,235 lines.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact-head Blacksmith Testbox lease: tbx_01kxdjewczyq45ncrfxey1s4tv\n- Core typecheck: node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core.tsbuildinfo\n- Focused tests: corepack pnpm test src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt.spawn-workspace.context-engine.test.ts\n- Result: 2 files passed, 197 tests passed\n- Deadcode export gate: passed\n- Autoreview after the CI-driven visibility fix: no accepted or actionable findings; patch correct at 0.99 confidence\n- Formatting and diff whitespace checks passed\n",
